 "notes": "Argument branches after structure into three parallel property lines (tensile/compressive strength, fracture, creep) that rejoin only in the inferred trade-off discussion. Image-vs-text discrepancies: (1) F1 b–f do not show grain boundaries, so the 65→22 µm grain sizes (n7) cannot be read from the figure; they are text-only claims attached to F1 (fit=poor). (2) F1 d–f visibly show particle clustering/streaking at 15–25 wt%, while text claims 'very few agglomerations'. (3) F3 shows UTS declining slightly (188→174 MPa) — text is silent; MatMech says 'unchanged'. (4) F7a lines converge/cross at 120 MPa: 5 and 10 wt% composites creep FASTER than AZ91 at high stress, not stated in text. (5) F2a at x150 shows needle/flake-like bright features that look unlike the equiaxed particles in F1; F2b 'clean interface' is asserted at x1500, which cannot resolve thin reaction layers. (6) F5 panels a/b look near-identical at x150; the 'brittle region increases with SiCp' claim is weakly supported. Lost: Table 1 numbers, stirring parameter rationale, the creep-stage discussion of F6. n24 (UTS-limiting mechanism) comes from MatMech extraction, not visible in packet text.",
 "migrated_from": "r01/graphs/Journal_of_Magnesium_and_Alloys__j.jma.2015.01.001.json"
}